Package: mp3rgain
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Lossless MP3 and AAC volume adjustment tool
 mp3rgain is a modern mp3gain and aacgain replacement written in Rust.
 It changes the volume of MP3 files and of AAC in M4A/MP4 or raw ADTS
 streams without re-encoding: only the global_gain field stored in each
 frame is rewritten, so the audio data is never decoded and compressed
 again. The command-line options, TSV output and undo tag follow mp3gain.
 .
 Features:
  - Track and album gain from ReplayGain analysis
  - ReplayGain 1.0 by default (mp3gain-identical values), with
    ReplayGain 2.0 and EBU R128 (ITU-R BS.1770) as options
  - REPLAYGAIN_* tagging, or tags only without changing the audio
  - Undo of gain changes (-u) from a stored tag
  - Recursive library scans with per-folder or per-release albums
  - Parallel processing, JSON and TSV output
